Protein Name: Hemoglobin subunit beta
Organism: Homo sapiens (Human)
UniProt Accession ID: P68871
Protein Function: Hemoglobin subunit beta combines with alpha chains to form adult hemoglobin. It binds oxygen in the lungs and transports it to tissues throughout the body while also helping transport carbon dioxide back to the lungs.
Cellular Location: Cytoplasm of erythrocytes (red blood cells).
